-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ז/3 — קיזוז שכר מעובדי הוראה בשל עיצומים/השבתות במערכת החינוך בשנת הלימודים תשס"ז (11.3.2007)
-- No salary for strike days: the owning body deducts it from each teacher
-- who took part, by the teacher's fixed timetable; the Ministry offsets the
-- owning bodies through the March 2007 payments.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `קיזוז שכר בשל עיצומים/השבתות תשס"ז`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 The letterhead, title, date, addressee and subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 The background: the teachers' organisations held sanctions and strikes in several localities; the dates follow in ¶12.

§§ `The strike dates`

@ref akn:hc_1/p12
`the strike dates` MEANS
    LIST Date 4 1 2007, Date 10 1 2007, Date 16 1 2007, Date 22 1 2007,
         Date 25 2 2007, Date 26 2 2007, Date 8 3 2007, Date 11 3 2007

GIVEN `day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a strike date` `day` IF
    elem `day` `the strike dates`

§§ `The deduction`

@desc One day of a teacher's fixed timetable at the school.
DECLARE `timetable day` HAS
    `calendar date`            IS A DATE
    `hours on the timetable`   IS A NUMBER  @desc the teacher's hours that day by the school's fixed timetable
    `took part in the strike`  IS A BOOLEAN

@desc A teacher, as far as this circular asks about them.
DECLARE `teacher record` HAS
    `days of the timetable`    IS A LIST OF `timetable day`
    `value of one hour`        IS A NUMBER  @desc the salary of one timetable hour; an input, not set by this circular

-- ¶13–14: by the State's decision no salary is paid to an employee who takes
-- part in the strike, so salary is deducted from every teacher who did.
-- ¶15: the owning body deducts by the teacher's fixed timetable at the school.
@ref akn:hc_1/p13 akn:hc_1/p14
GIVEN d IS A `timetable day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no salary is paid for` d IF
        d's `took part in the strike`
    AND `is a strike date` (d's `calendar date`)

@ref akn:hc_1/p15
GIVEN t IS A `teacher record`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours to deduct` t IS
    sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD d's `hours on the timetable`)
             (filter (GIVEN d YIELD `no salary is paid for` d) (t's `days of the timetable`)))

GIVEN t IS A `teacher record`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary to deduct` t IS
    `hours to deduct` t TIMES t's `value of one hour`

DECLARE `strike action` IS ONE OF
    `deduct the salary` HAS `amount deducted` IS A NUMBER
    `offset the owning body's payments` HAS `hours offset` IS A NUMBER

-- The owning body's duty to deduct (¶13–15). The circular sets no date for it.
GIVEN t IS A `teacher record`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the owning body deducts the strike salary` t IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `deduct the salary` amount
          PROVIDED amount AT LEAST `salary to deduct` t

-- Time in months from March 2007 (0): the Ministry offsets the owning
-- bodies through the March 2007 standing-payment (מת"מ) transfers, by the
-- budgeted hours of the striking institutions and the dates and localities
-- of the strike (¶16–17). The hours are the Ministry's figure: an input.
@ref akn:hc_1/p16 akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN `budgeted hours of the striking institutions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the Ministry offsets the strike` `budgeted hours of the striking institutions` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `offset the owning body's payments` h
          PROVIDED h EQUALS `budgeted hours of the striking institutions`
    WITHIN 1

-- akn:hc_1/p18 Notice that a further circular on later sanctions will be sent separately; no rule.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

-- Examples; the hour value of 100 is a placeholder.
`a teacher who struck twice` MEANS
    `teacher record` WITH
        `days of the timetable` IS
            LIST `timetable day` (Date 4 1 2007) 5 TRUE,
                 `timetable day` (Date 5 1 2007) 6 FALSE,
                 `timetable day` (Date 10 1 2007) 4 TRUE,
                 `timetable day` (Date 16 1 2007) 5 FALSE
        `value of one hour` IS 100

#ASSERT `hours to deduct` `a teacher who struck twice` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `salary to deduct` `a teacher who struck twice` EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `is a strike date` (Date 25 2 2007)
#ASSERT NOT `is a strike date` (Date 24 2 2007)

#TRACE `the owning body deducts the strike salary` `a teacher who struck twice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `deduct the salary` 900 AT 1
#TRACE `the Ministry offsets the strike` 40 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `offset the owning body's payments` 40 AT 1
